# tools/round_paint_witness.rish -- a source pattern ROUNDED to fill a box, whole copies scaled to fit, proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the fourth and last member of the CSS background-repeat family, sibling to
# tools/compose_tiled_witness.rish (repeat, clips the boundary), tools/space_paint_witness.rish (space, ground gaps), and
# tools/place_paint_witness.rish (no-repeat, one anchored copy). Where those tile at the pattern's native size, round
# RESIZES each copy so a whole count paves the box exactly -- no gap and no clip. It composes over image/scale.rye (the
# nearest-neighbor resize) and image/compose.rye (the src-over blit), adding no new resample, no color math, no codec.
# Design read: active-designing/20260816-210735_season-g-color-algebra-crux.md (the open-media floor this joins).
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: gratitude/w3c-css-color.md (the W3C CSS spec -- public standards only).
#
# The crux this witness proves is that round SCALES the tile rather than clipping or gapping it: an exact fit rounds to a
# clean identity repeat; a non-dividing 3x2 box scales the copies (cell 0 the identity 2x2, cell 1 the pattern shrunk to
# 1x2) so the whole box is paved with no gap and no clip; a 4x4 pattern larger than a 2x2 box shrinks to one copy sampling
# all four corners (a resize, never a clipped window); a translucent pattern blends src-over uniform; the rounded image
# round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte; a sub-rectangle rounds only its own box; a zero dimension, an empty
# pattern, and an out-of-bounds box each refuse by name having painted nothing. Compose not braid -- scale owns the resize,
# compose owns the blit, qoi owns the buffers; this rung only routes the box into whole cells. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/round_paint_witness.rish

say "round_paint: Language EN -- Season G's background-repeat: round; a keeper names a box and a pattern and reads back the box paved with whole, resized copies, none clipped and none gapped, on our own open geometry and codec."
say "round_paint: Style Radiant -- compose not braid; image/scale.rye owns the resize and image/compose.rye owns the blit, and this rung only ROUTES the box into a whole count of cells and paints each a resized copy, so a whole number of copies pave the box with no gap and no clip."
say "round_paint: Lens TAME -- the whole box bound-checked ONCE up front (in u64) BEFORE any tile is resized; the count a pure per-axis rule (round(box/unit), at least one); the box split into a fair integer partition whose cells differ by at most one pixel; at most four distinct tile sizes resized; all-or-nothing so a refusal allocates and paints nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/round_paint"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/round_paint.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "round_paint: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "round_paint: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "round_paint: ${out}"

# Check the GREEN claim with Rishi's native `contains`, never a shell grep over interpolated output -- an apostrophe in
# the selftest prose can never close a shell quote here, the loom REDS %76/%85 taught the tree.
assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-round" else "round_paint: selftest did not print the GREEN round line"

say "round_paint: GREEN -- a source pattern rounded to fill a box, whole copies resized so a whole count pave it exactly, proven on metal: an exact fit rounded to a clean identity repeat; a non-dividing 3x2 box scaled the copies with no gap and no clip; a 4x4 pattern larger than a 2x2 box shrank to one copy sampling all four corners; a translucent pattern blended src-over uniform; a byte-for-byte QOI round trip; a sub-rectangle rounded only its own box; and every malformed fill refused by name having painted nothing."
